Well some of this could be much easier for a computer then a player. For
example you could simply program it to not eat things that have been dead
over 49 turns. The computer isn't going to miscount. You could program in
the exceptions. If you wrote the bot spoiled with what gives what then it
would be no problem at all.
On the other hand the early game is under an odd kind of timer. You have
limited food. And staying at the same spot forever hoping for some item or
resistence could lead to starving to death. If you built the bot to be a
learning model then you could end up with odd situations like the bot
refusing to go past level 4 because one game it met a gnome with a wand of
death, and it won't descend without a way to face it.

